    "explanation": "Rider, your SGD 4.00 no-show charge is refunded in full. Driver, no compensation is payable.\n\nTHE FEE CANNOT STAND. To be chargeable under POL-NS-01 all four limbs must hold together. Limb (c) fails on arithmetic measured the way the clause insists — from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix, not from the 'arrived' tap. The driver's own trace shows one continuous in-geofence run of 40 seconds (21:46:50 to 21:47:30, 5 fixes at 10 s cadence) against the 300-second minimum for a LARGE_VENUE pickup: a shortfall of 260 seconds. Limb (d) also fails: the trip record shows cancelled_by 'SYSTEM' and cancellation_reason_code 'SYSTEM_TIMEOUT', not a driver termination on RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT. Under POL-NS-06 the cancellation-fee line is therefore refunded in full, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not she answered messages. The only route that could sum separate in-geofence intervals, POL-NS-06(i), is unavailable: the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00601-01 is MISSING with no payload and weight 0.0 (issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), so holding position was lawfully possible and the single 40-second run is the whole of the dwell. POL-NS-04 reaches the same result independently — the rider sent a locating message at 21:47:50 inside the waiting window, the driver never replied within 120 seconds and trip_record.in_app_calls is empty, and the rider's device sat within the LARGE_VENUE 150 m presence radius for all 41 qualifying fixes.\n\nNO DRIVER COMPENSATION. POL-NS-07 pays 80 percent of the fee only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it; both preconditions fail here. The anti-farming check does not trip in any event (no_show_terminations_30d = 1 against completed_trips_30d = 110, a rate of about 0.009), so no escalation arises on that limb.\n\nTHE ARRIVAL ITSELF WAS GENUINE, AND THERE IS NO FALSE-ARRIVAL REFERRAL. The trace places the driver stationary inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius at the arrival timestamp, with a minimum distance to the pin of 9.27 m, so POL-NS-05 is not engaged and POL-NS-05(ii) cannot fire: the trip is not recorded as a false-arrival event. The SGD 4.00 figure reconciles exactly with the fee_schedule resolution rule — the greater of the LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00) — and is precisely the ledger's cancellation-fee line, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare-integrity defect; the refund is the cancellation-fee line only.\n\nDriver, your account that the passenger was not at the pin is not supported by the rider's telemetry, which places her within 19.5 m of the pin, stationary, for the whole wait. That the two other people boarded does not change the fee outcome, and no clause in this category produces a referral on that point; if the platform wishes to look at why the vehicle left a live booking, that is a question for its own channels, not a referral this ruling can order.\n\nCONFIDENCE AND INTEGRITY. The deciding facts — the 40-second dwell and the SYSTEM_TIMEOUT termination — are carried by the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00601) and the trip record (EV-TRIP-00601), both at weight 1.0 and both independent of each other. Neither is impaired under POL-NS-08(a)–(d): no clock skew (arrived 21:46:55 sits within one 10 s fix of the trace), no sampling gap over 120 seconds, 72 fixes with 100 percent coverage, the chat holds exactly the 2 messages trip_record.chat_message_count records, and the fee line reconciles. Confidence is 0.95, above the 0.70 floor, so no escalation."
